<p>
  Bathroom remodel costs in Plano vary widely depending on scope, and most of the difference comes down to three things: whether you are changing the layout, what finishes you choose, and whether the room is a full bath or a master.
</p>

<h2>Typical bathroom remodel ranges in Plano</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Full bathroom remodel:</strong> roughly <strong>$20,000–$30,000</strong> for a complete project — demo, new tile, vanity, fixtures, lighting, and paint.</li>
  <li><strong>Master bathroom remodel:</strong> roughly <strong>$30,000–$50,000</strong>, reflecting larger square footage, bigger showers, double vanities, and higher-end finishes.</li>
  <li><strong>High-end master baths:</strong> can reach <strong>$75,000+</strong> with premium tile, custom cabinetry, and extensive plumbing changes.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What drives the price up</h2>
<h3>Layout changes</h3>
<p>
  Moving a toilet, shower, or vanity means relocating plumbing, which is the single biggest cost driver in a bathroom remodel. Keeping fixtures near their existing drain and supply lines keeps both cost and timeline in check.
</p>
<h3>Tile and finish quality</h3>
<p>
  Tile is usually the largest line item in a bathroom. Large-format tile, natural stone, and intricate patterns cost more in material and labor than standard options — but they are also where a bathroom's look is made.
</p>
<h3>Scope of work</h3>
<p>
  A focused update (replacing a vanity and fixtures in place) is different from a full gut. If your goal is simply a fresher look with new fixtures and paint, you may not need a full remodel at all. We are always upfront about which projects actually warrant the full scope.
</p>

<h2>Popular upgrades worth planning for</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Garden tub to walk-in shower conversions</strong> — one of the most requested changes in Plano. See our guide to <a href="/blog/garden-tub-to-walk-in-shower-plano/">garden tub conversions</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Double vanities</strong> — a practical upgrade for shared master baths.</li>
  <li><strong>Walk-in showers with glass panels</strong> — easier to use and easier to clean than tub-and-shower combos.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Getting an accurate number</h2>
<p>
  Ranges like these are a useful starting point, but your actual estimate depends on your home — especially if it is an older home in East Plano where walls and plumbing can hide surprises. A <a href="/contact/">free consultation</a> gives you an itemized estimate for your specific bathroom, and our <a href="/cost-guides/">cost guides</a> explain exactly what is included and what is not.
</p>
